: "The narrower gap among independents noted in mid-October coverage could tighten the race if late-breaking voters break against the incumbent.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Seth Magaziner (D) is running."]}, "overview": "First-term incumbent Seth Magaziner seeks reelection in a Rhode Island district that leans Democratic by about four points. Two October polls of likely voters show him leading Republican Vic Mellor by 13 to 16 points, and prediction markets give him roughly a 96% chance of winning. Mellor won a contested GOP primary in September but enters the general election with only about $44,000 on hand after spending heavily to secure the nomination, while Magaziner holds a large cash advantage. The national political environment favors Democrats this cycle, adding to the incumbent's structural edge. Magaziner's lead among independents is narrower than his overall margin, which is the main source of residual uncertainty, but all available evidence points to a comfortable Democratic hold in this seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9811, "margin": 17.36}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9798, "margin": 17.4}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9847, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9785, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9853, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9758, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9766, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9771, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.97, "margin": 16.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9714, "margin": 16.5}, {"date":